The structure templates in this folder are copied from data/stonevaults/structure/ in that jar: the
pieces of its dungeon and pillager dungeon (entrances, lobbies, rooms, stairways, treasure rooms). Each
room's YAML sidecar names its source file.

Changed by Realmforge (2026-10-14), with `rf rooms import` and the rules in
art/rooms/stonevaults/rules.yaml of the Realmforge repository:
- minecraft:chain renamed to minecraft:iron_chain, its name since Minecraft 1.21.9;
- structure blocks left from the authoring world removed;
- jigsaws inside a room (mob and blocker stubs) replaced by the block they leave behind, and the
  connectors renamed realmforge:door (sides) and realmforge:shaft (up, down);
- the containers' loot tables and every entity except paintings and item frames removed;
- the rooms other than the entrances given more block variety (mossy, cracked and gravel variants on plain
  floors, walls and ceilings) and decorations (vines, cobwebs, barrels, armor stands on stone brick stairs);
- templates written back in a normalized form (blocks sorted, stored deflate).
